  "basis": "The ob_check for r1 refutes the B condition because it misreads the color-to-risk mapping. The legend explicitly maps dark maroon to 'Low' (0) and pale yellow to 'High' (100). Therefore, Illinois (IL), colored pale yellow, is the highest-risk state among the three options. Kansas (KS), colored dark maroon, is the lowest-risk. Delaware (DE), colored orange, is medium-risk. The task requires selecting the highest-risk state, which is Illinois.",
